1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,883
先俯瞰，再缓缓转成斜视：原本并排的功能可以上下堆叠，缩短某些晶粒间的路径。
Begin overhead, then tilt: functions can be stacked rather than placed side by side, shortening selected die-to-die routes.

2
00:00:11,883 --> 00:00:20,169
这不是把完整电路板直接叠起来，而是在精密控制的界面接合晶粒。
This is not a stack of circuit boards. Dies meet at carefully controlled interfaces.

3
00:00:20,169 --> 00:00:30,000
先数清有几层，再找每一层的角色。
Count the layers and identify what each layer contributes before inspecting the bond.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:41,874
上层可以放计算或存储功能，下层可以承接其他电路与连接；具体配置取决于架构。
Upper and lower dies can divide compute, memory and connection functions in different ways. Architecture determines which functions belong together.

5
00:00:41,874 --> 00:00:46,043
堆叠不保证每层都使用同一工艺。
Their process technologies need not match.

6
00:00:46,043 --> 00:01:00,000
这里是通用教学模型，不是 SoIC 或 Foveros 特定产品的内部配置图。
This is a generic teaching model, not an internal floorplan of a particular SoIC or Foveros product.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:11,919
靠近界面：铜接点建立电性连接，周围介电表面也参与接合，这就是混合键合的关键。
Approach the interface: copper contacts provide electrical connections while surrounding dielectric surfaces also bond. That combination defines hybrid bonding.

8
00:01:11,919 --> 00:01:30,000
不要把它画成一排大型焊球；焊料微凸块与直接混合键合是不同的互连方式，适用限制也不同。
Do not picture a row of large solder balls. Solder microbumps and direct hybrid bonding are different interconnect approaches with different integration constraints.

9
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,832
让两片晶粒暂时分离，想象任何微粒或表面不平都可能留在接合界面。
Separate the dies and imagine a particle or uneven surface trapped between them.

10
00:01:39,832 --> 00:01:47,017
表面准备、洁净度、平坦度与对位精度共同决定质量。
Surface preparation, cleanliness, flatness and alignment work together to determine bond quality.

11
00:01:47,017 --> 00:02:00,000
动画把动作放慢是为了看懂原理，不提供清洗配方或工艺温度。
The motion is slowed to explain the principle; it is not a cleaning recipe or a manufacturing temperature schedule.

12
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:08,614
分层示意中的接合距离虽短，数据仍要经过晶粒内部电路与布线。
The bond interface is short, but data still traverses circuits and wiring within each die.

13
00:02:08,614 --> 00:02:15,476
垂直连接只解决路径的一部分，不会让逻辑延迟消失。
Vertical connectivity solves only part of the path; it does not remove logic delay.

14
00:02:15,476 --> 00:02:30,000
找出跨越接合面的那一步，再把它放回完整的信号链。
Identify the crossing between dies, then place that crossing back into the complete signal chain.

15
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:38,660
密集接点能让相邻层交换更多信息，但架构必须真的用得上这些连接。
Dense contacts can support richer communication between layers, but the architecture must make use of them.

16
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:47,665
先决定数据分工，再规划接点与供电，不要先堆出最多接点才找用途。
Define the division of data and work before allocating contacts and power. More connections are not a goal by themselves.

17
00:02:47,665 --> 00:03:00,000
画面中的流动是信息关系示意，没有宣称特定速度。
Animated movement shows information relationships, not a claimed transfer speed.

18
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,934
从侧面看热往外走的路径。
From the side, follow heat out of the stack.

19
00:03:03,934 --> 00:03:11,335
不同层的发热位置、界面热阻与散热器位置共同影响温度。
Heat-source location, interface resistance and cooler placement jointly affect temperature.

20
00:03:11,335 --> 00:03:30,000
不能认为堆叠越高就越好；把最热的电路放在哪里，是一开始就要解决的架构问题。
A taller stack is not automatically better. Where the hottest circuits belong is an architectural decision to make early, not a problem to postpone until assembly.

21
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:39,100
被其他晶粒盖住的接点不容易再直接碰到，因此要预先设计测试访问。
Contacts become difficult to reach after another die covers them, so test access must be designed in advance.

22
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:46,327
组装前筛选、接合后连通检查与系统测试各有任务。
Pre-assembly screening, post-bond connectivity and system testing serve different purposes.

23
00:03:46,327 --> 00:04:00,000
通过一次测试不是永久保证；要把覆盖率与剩余风险说清楚。
One passing test is not a permanent guarantee; coverage and remaining risk must be explicit.

24
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:09,075
拉开到整体视角，高密度集成会同时提高界面质量与测试规划的重要性。
Zoom out: dense integration makes interface quality and test planning more important.

25
00:04:09,075 --> 00:04:16,333
已接合的晶粒未必能经济地拆换，所以前段筛选更有价值。
Bonded dies may not be economical to replace, increasing the value of earlier screening.

26
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:30,000
比较方案时，要连同良品成本、热条件与返修能力一起看。
Compare solutions using cost per good unit, thermal conditions and repair options together, rather than connection density alone.

27
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:41,625
最后的路线是功能分层、界面设计、表面准备、对位接合、可测试性与散热验证。
The route is functional partitioning, interface design, surface preparation, alignment, bonding, testability and thermal verification.

28
00:04:41,625 --> 00:05:00,000
记住：3D 的重点不是把楼盖高，而是让最需要沟通的功能靠近，同时让电流、热与测试都有可靠出口。
The aim of 3D is not merely a taller building. It is to bring communicating functions closer while preserving dependable paths for electricity, heat and testing.
